            <ArticleTitle>Atresia of the distal external acoustic meatus in a Bouvier des Flandres.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>88-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A five-year-old male Bouvier des Flandres was presented with chronic otalgia of approximately four and a half years' duration. Atresia of the external acoustic meatus was diagnosed. A total ear canal ablation and bulla osteotomy were performed. All symptoms of otalgia resolved within two weeks of surgery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
